WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:18.208
A young gazelle walked across the savanna.

2
00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:36.793
He ate some grass and a few leaves.

3
00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:40.071
The sun felt very hot.

4
00:00:40.071 --> 00:00:42.803
"I'm thirsty," said the gazelle.

5
00:00:42.803 --> 00:00:47.758
"I'll go to the water hole."

6
00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:56.547
When the gazelle reached the water hole, he took a few sips.

7
00:00:56.547 --> 00:01:00.820
Then he looked up.

8
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:06.540
Another young animal was watching the gazelle.

9
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.562
The animal had sharp teeth and claws.

10
00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:20.145
But he didn't look mean.

11
00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:47.255
The two animals playfully chased each other.

12
00:01:47.255 --> 00:01:59.633
They splashed in the water.

13
00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:08.493
When the sun began to set, the gazelle headed home.

14
00:02:08.493 --> 00:02:12.498
He told his mother about his new friend.

15
00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.789
"What did he look like?" she asked.

16
00:02:15.789 --> 00:02:27.666
The gazelle told her.

17
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:30.722
"He's a lion!" she said.

18
00:02:30.722 --> 00:02:33.664
"You can't be friends with him!"

19
00:02:33.664 --> 00:02:36.972
"Why not?" asked the gazelle.

20
00:02:36.972 --> 00:02:39.457
"Well," said his mother.

21
00:02:39.457 --> 00:02:41.915
"Gazelles are herbivores.

22
00:02:41.915 --> 00:02:46.958
That means we eat plants.

23
00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.645
But lions are carnivores.

24
00:02:49.645 --> 00:02:53.509
They eat meat."

25
00:02:53.509 --> 00:02:56.039
"Meat?" said the gazelle.

26
00:02:56.039 --> 00:02:59.138
"Like other animals?"

27
00:02:59.138 --> 00:03:02.234
"Yes," said his mother.

28
00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:08.820
"The other day I saw a jackal eating berries," said the gazelle.

29
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.504
"Can I be friends with him?"

30
00:03:11.504 --> 00:03:13.857
"No," said his mother.

31
00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:16.295
"Jackals are omnivores.

32
00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:20.301
They eat some plants.

33
00:03:20.301 --> 00:03:25.917
But they also eat other animals."

34
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:30.752
"Meat eaters are terrible!" said the gazelle.

35
00:03:30.752 --> 00:03:34.463
"No, they're not terrible," said his mother.

36
00:03:34.463 --> 00:03:37.912
"That's just how the food chain works."

37
00:03:37.912 --> 00:03:40.923
"Food chain?" asked the gazelle.

38
00:03:40.923 --> 00:03:43.404
"Yes," said his mother.

39
00:03:43.404 --> 00:03:47.218
"All living things need food for energy.

40
00:03:47.218 --> 00:03:52.919
Plants get their energy from sunlight.

41
00:03:52.919 --> 00:04:03.340
We get our energy from eating plants.

42
00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:12.785
And meat eaters get it from eating other animals."

43
00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.502
"I guess I understand," said the gazelle.

44
00:04:16.502 --> 00:04:20.405
"Too bad that lion is a meat eater.

45
00:04:20.405 --> 00:04:32.865
We had so much fun."

